{"patch":{"config":{"title":"Antranig Basman","baseURL":"https://ponder.org.uk","defaultContentLanguage":"en","mainSections":["post","posts"],"author":{"name":"Antranig Basman","website":"/","email":"amb26web@ponder.org.uk","twitter":"amb26ponder"},"params":{"homeTitle":"Antranig Basman","subtitle":"Building habitable technologies","bio":"img/20230209_135356 - bio - cropped.jpg","logo":"img/pond.jpg","favicon":"img/favicon.ico","dateFormat":"January 2, 2006","comments":true,"socialShare":true,"showRelatedPosts":true,"commentsLayer":"beautifulWend.comments.giscus","customCSS":["css/ponder.css"],"mediaIcons":[{"title":"Twitter profile","href":"http://twitter.com/amb26ponder","icon":"fab fa-twitter"},{"title":"Send me a message","href":"mailto:amb26webpage@ponder.org.uk","icon":"fa fa-envelope"},{"title":"Antranig's GitHub profile","href":"http://github.com/amb26","icon":"fab fa-github-alt"},{"title":"My papers on DBLP","href":"https://dblp.org/pid/68/5013.html","icon":"fa fa-university"},{"title":"My LinkedIn profile","href":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/antranigbasman/","icon":"fab fa-linkedin"}],"giscus":{"repo":"amb26/ponder","repoId":"R_kgDOOKllGA","category":"Announcements","categoryId":"DIC_kwDOOKllGM4CvhAS"}},"menu":{"main":[{"name":"Posts","url":"post","weight":1},{"name":"WiP","url":"wip","weight":1},{"name":"Docs","identifier":"docs","url":"docs","weight":3},{"name":"Fluid Signals","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-signals","weight":1},{"name":"Fluid Integration Language","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-integration-language","weight":2},{"name":"Fluid View","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-view","weight":3},{"name":"Fluid PTF","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-ptf","weight":4},{"name":"Fluid tldraw integration","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-tldraw","weight":5},{"name":"wend","parent":"docs","url":"docs/wend","weight":6},{"name":"About","url":"page/about/","weight":3},{"name":"Communities","url":"communities","weight":4},{"name":"Projects","url":"projects","weight":5},{"name":"Terms","url":"term","weight":5}]}},"features":{"selfHosted":true,"hljs":true}},"pages":[{"kind":"page","type":"page","section":"","title":"My Projects","relPermalink":"/projects/","permalink":"https://ponder.org.uk/projects/","outputPath":"/projects/index.html","params":{"title":"My Projects"},"sourcePath":"content/projects.md","content":"<div class=\"community-row\" id=\"melittoflora\">\n  <div class=\"community-picture\">\n  <a href=\"https://agsci.oregonstate.edu/bee-atlas\">\n    <img height=\"100px\" src=\"/img/beeatlas-logo3-03.jpg\"/>\n    </a>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"community-desc\">\nSince 2022 I have worked for the \n<a href=\"https://agsci.oregonstate.edu/bee-atlas\">Oregon Bee Atlas</a> to help landowners understand plant-pollinator\ninteractions and guide their land use decisions including evaluation of seed mixes, as well as supporting their\nvolunteers' observation work. I have implemented the \n<a href=\"https://oregon-bee-project.github.io/melittoflora/viz.html\">Melittoflora</a> tool using a provisional version \nof the Infusion framework which filters the project's data on wild bees by geographical, temporal and taxonomic filters and \nvisualises the resulting interactions as a live, attractive bipartite ribbon graph. \n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"community-row\">\n  <div class=\"community-picture\">\n  <a href=\"/infusion\">\n    <img height=\"100px\" src=\"/img/infusion.png\"/>\n    </a>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"community-desc\">\n<p>Since 2008 I have been the lead developer of the <a href=\"/infusion\">Infusion</a> framework, a JavaScript framework supporting\nthe development of flexible software. Versions 1 through 4 of Infusion were relatively conventionally structured libraries supporting the development\nof various UI widgets. Since 2024 a <a href=\"https://github.com/fluid-project/infusion-6\">comprehensive rewrite</a> of Infusion has been underway for version 6\nbased on reactive primitives throughout, structuring it as a <a href=\"/term/substrate\">software substrate</a> constituting\nan <a href=\"/term/integration-domain\">integration domain</a>.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"community-row\">\n  <div class=\"community-picture\">\n  <a href=\"https://files.eric.ed.gov/fulltext/ED562223.pdf\">\n    <img height=\"100px\" src=\"/img/MoS.jpg\"/>\n    </a>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"community-desc\">\nIn 2012 I was lucky enough to work with the late great <a href=\"https://www.colorado.edu/atlas/michael-eisenberg\">Mike Eisenberg</a>\nto produce an incarnation of Hal Abelson and Andy diSessa's \n<a href=\"https://direct.mit.edu/books/oa-monograph/4663/chapter/213442/Turtle-Escapes-the-Plane\">spherical turtle concept</a> \nto run on NOAA's <a href=\"https://sos.noaa.gov/\">Science on a Sphere</a> planetarium system. I wrote WebGL \n<a href=\"https://github.com/Math-on-a-Sphere/Math-on-a-Sphere/blob/master/MathClient/src/main/webapp/shaders/generalPolygon.c\">shader code</a> to rasterise\nspherical polygons into the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Equirectangular_projection\">ECE projection system</a> accepted by the projectors and worked on a Logo-like language to invoke it. You can\ntry out an <a href=\"/weblogo/client.html\">in-browser implementation of WebLogo here</a>.\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"community-row\">\n  <div class=\"community-picture\">\n  <a href=\"https://gpii.net/\">\n    <img height=\"100px\" src=\"/img/gpii-logo.jpg\"/>\n    </a>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"community-desc\">\nFrom 2010 to 2020 I was core framework architect for the <a href=\"https://gpii.net/\">GPII</a> \n(now <a href=\"https://morphic.org/\">Morphic</a>), an autopersonalization project aiming to automatically adapt technology to meet the \nneeds and preferences of users. A description of our architecture and goals appeared in a <a href=\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-07509-9_35\">HCI 2014 paper</a>.\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"community-row\">\n  <div class=\"community-picture\">\n  <a href=\"https://darwin-online.org.uk\">\n    <img height=\"100px\" src=\"/img/darwin-online.jpg\"/>\n    </a>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"community-desc\">\nEarly deployments of the RSF framework were the twinned <a href=\"https://darwin-online.org.uk\">Darwin Online</a> and\n<a href=\"https://wallace-online.org/\">Wallace Online</a> projects. Darwin Online is the world's largest resource on Charles Darwin\nand has served over a billion documents since being deployed in 2006, despite not receiving external funding since 2008 \n(when the codebase was last updated). It exemplifies the \"plain documents\" ethic of our movement and is managed via CSV files and HTML exports from DreamWeaver\nrather than a heavyweight CMS.\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"community-row\">\n  <div class=\"community-picture\">\n  <a href=\"https://rsf.github.io/wiki/Wikib2ab.html?page=Main\">\n    <img height=\"100px\" src=\"/img/rsf.png\"/>\n    </a>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"community-desc\">\nMy first outing in the space of web technologies, <a href=\"https://rsf.github.io/wiki/Wikib2ab.html?page=Main\">RSF</a>\n(2005-2008) was an unusual kind of Java framework which developed a dialect \nof <a href=\"https://rsf.github.io/wiki/Wikicce8.html?page=PureXHTMLTemplating\">logic-free HTML templates</a> against a backend\nof demand-driven dataflow defined in the\n<a href=\"https://docs.spring.io/spring-framework/docs/3.0.x/spring-framework-reference/html/beans.html\">Spring configuration format</a>.\nThe intention was to leverage the then-prevalent ecosystem of plain HTML authoring tools such as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adobe_Dreamweaver\">Dreamweaver</a>\nin a strategy whose faults are written up in my 2021 PPIG paper on <a href=\"https://ppig.org/files/2021-PPIG-32nd-basman.pdf\">Markup-driven polymorphism</a>.\n</div>\n</div>\n","summary":"Since 2022 I have worked for the Oregon Bee Atlas to help landowners understand plant-pollinator interactions and guide their land use decisions including evaluation of seed mixes, as well as supporting their volunteers' observation work. I have implemented the Melittoflora tool using a provisional version of the Infusion framework which filters the project's data on wild bees by geographical, temporal and taxonomic filters and visualises the resulting interactions as a live, attractive bipartite ribbon graph.","summaryText":"Since 2022 I have worked for the Oregon Bee Atlas to help landowners understand plant-pollinator interactions and guide their land use decisions including evaluation of seed mixes, as well as supporting their volunteers' observation work. I have implemented the Melittoflora tool using a provisional version of the Infusion framework which filters the project's data on wild bees by geographical, temporal and taxonomic filters and visualises the resulting interactions as a live, attractive bipartite ribbon graph.","truncated":true,"nextInSection":{"title":"Infusion","relPermalink":"/infusion/"}}],"shared":{"lang":"en","menu":[{"name":"Posts","url":"post","weight":1,"children":[]},{"name":"WiP","url":"wip","weight":1,"children":[]},{"name":"About","url":"page/about/","weight":3,"children":[]},{"name":"Docs","identifier":"docs","url":"docs","weight":3,"children":[{"name":"Fluid Signals","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-signals","weight":1,"children":[]},{"name":"Fluid Integration Language","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-integration-language","weight":2,"children":[]},{"name":"Fluid View","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-view","weight":3,"children":[]},{"name":"Fluid PTF","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-ptf","weight":4,"children":[]},{"name":"Fluid tldraw integration","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-tldraw","weight":5,"children":[]},{"name":"wend","parent":"docs","url":"docs/wend","weight":6,"children":[]}]},{"name":"Communities","url":"communities","weight":4,"children":[]},{"name":"Projects","url":"projects","weight":5,"children":[]},{"name":"T